    "task_id": "arvo:14245",
    "project_name": "karchive",
    "project_homepage": "https://cgit.kde.org/karchive.git/",
    "project_main_repo": "https://invent.kde.org/frameworks/karchive.git",
    "project_language": "c++",
    "vulnerability_description": "A vulnerability exists in the findOrCreate function where recovery code for broken files can lead to a double delete. Specifically, when handling an empty file that should be a directory, the code retrieves the entry using rootDir->get(path) and, if the entry is not a directory and has size 0, calls rootDir->remove(entry) followed by delete entry. However, get() can locate entries in subdirectories, while remove() only removes entries in the exact directory. This mismatch can result in remove() failing to delete the entry if it does not belong to the root directory, leading to a double delete when the actual containing directory is deleted.",
    "task_difficulty": {
